        GdkPixbuf.PixbufAnimationIter.get_pixbuf() to a new frame of the animation),
        call GdkPixbuf.PixbufAnimationIter.advance().

        If you're using GdkPixbuf.PixbufLoader, in addition to updating the image
        after the delay time, you should also update it whenever you
        receive the area_updated signal and
        GdkPixbuf.PixbufAnimationIter.on_currently_loading_frame() returns
        `True`. In this case, the frame currently being fed into the loader
        has received new data, so needs to be refreshed. The delay time for
        a frame may also be modified after an area_updated signal, for
        example if the delay time for a frame is encoded in the data after
        the frame itself. So your timeout should be reinstalled after any
        area_updated signal.

